#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Priority 6: superlevel topology robustness evaluation on EXISTING PhIRE
outputs only.

This script does NOT retrain anything and does NOT modify any existing
candidate output or any existing (sublevel/default) TTK topology output. It
only reads already-completed dataGT.npy / dataSR.npy / idx.npy / dataIN.npy
arrays and produces a brand-new, separate superlevel topology evaluation.

Mathematical basis
-------------------
TTK's ttkPersistenceDiagramCmd / ttkMergeTreeCmd (as invoked everywhere else
in this repo, e.g. scripts/run_candidate_topology_pipeline.sh) compute
SUBLEVEL-set topology by default -- no sublevel/superlevel flag is ever
passed anywhere in this codebase. The standard identity

    superlevel topology of a scalar field s  ==  sublevel topology of -s

(persistence pairs, critical points, and merge trees are exactly
mirror-imaged under negation) means we can get a robust superlevel
evaluation using the exact same TTK binaries, unmodified, by feeding them a
NEGATED speed field instead of a superlevel-specific code path. This is the
approach used here: every VTI written by this script stores -speed, not
speed, and is then processed by the SAME ttkPersistenceDiagramCmd /
ttkMergeTreeCmd commands used for the default (sublevel) evaluation.

VTI array-name convention
--------------------------
The VTK point-data array is still named "wind_speed" (matching
scripts/convert_phire_to_vti.py and every existing TTK invocation, which
all hardcode `-a wind_speed`), so the unmodified `-a wind_speed` TTK CLI
flag keeps working unchanged. IMPORTANT: despite the array name, the stored
scalar values are -sqrt(u^2 + v^2), i.e. NEGATED speed, not speed. This is
intentional and is what makes the sublevel-set TTK computation equal a
superlevel-set computation on the original (non-negated) speed field.

VTI flattening convention
--------------------------
Uses the exact same C-order flattening as scripts/convert_phire_to_vti.py's
make_vti_from_scalar(): a (H, W) array is written with
`ravel(order="C")`, and vtkImageData.SetDimensions(W, H, 1) is used, so
flat[ix + iy*W] == scalar_2d[iy, ix]. This is the repaired VTI convention
established in docs/candidateD_E_topology_audit.md Section 2.3 (an earlier
Fortran-order bug silently transposed/scrambled every written field).

Patch convention
-----------------
Uses the same 160x160 patch at (x0=0, y0=0) as every other topology
pipeline in this repo (scripts/run_candidate_topology_pipeline.sh,
scripts/run_topology_pipeline.sh both default --patch 160 --x0 0 --y0 0),
so superlevel results are directly comparable to the existing sublevel
results for the same methods.

Output isolation
-----------------
All outputs are written under a brand-new root,
ttk_runs_fixed/superlevel_topology/, which is disjoint from every existing
sublevel topology root (ttk_runs_fixed/topology_finetuning/,
ttk_runs_fixed/cnn/, ttk_runs_fixed/gan/, ttk_runs_fixed/combined/). This
script asserts that disjointness at startup and refuses to run if it is
ever violated. It only ever READS from data_out*/models*/ candidate output
directories, never writes to them.

Methods evaluated (first superlevel robustness set)
-----------------------------------------------------
  cnn                                              data_out_fixed/wind_mrhr_cnn
  gan                                              data_out_fixed/wind_mrhr_gan
  candidateC_expanded2688                          data_out/wind_finetune_candidateC_expanded2688
  candidateB_plus_E2_tf_lowlambda_expanded2688      data_out/wind_finetune_candidateB_plus_E2_tf_lowlambda_expanded2688
  candidateC_plus_E2_tf_lowlambda_expanded2688      data_out/wind_finetune_candidateC_plus_E2_tf_lowlambda_expanded2688
  candidateUV_plus_E2_tf_lowlambda_expanded2688     data_out/wind_finetune_candidateUV_plus_E2_tf_lowlambda_expanded2688
  candidateUV_plus_crit_expanded2688                data_out/wind_finetune_candidateUV_plus_crit_expanded2688

NOTE on candidateC_plus_E2_tf_lowlambda_expanded2688: this literal directory
name is what was specified for this priority. Elsewhere in this repo the
completed "Candidate C stack + repaired E2" native-TF run is named
candidateE2_tf_lowlambda_expanded2688 (see
scripts/run_candidateE2_tf_lowlambda_expanded2688_ttkcrit_refiner.py), with
real output at data_out/wind_finetune_candidateE2_tf_lowlambda_expanded2688.
Both names refer to the same experiment ("C + E2"), but this script does
NOT silently alias them -- it looks up exactly the path in DEFAULT_METHODS
and, per the "warn and skip" requirement below, will print a clear warning
and skip this entry if that literal directory does not exist. If you intend
to evaluate the real C+E2-2688 run, either edit DEFAULT_METHODS below or use
--methods to exclude this entry and evaluate it under a corrected mapping.

If any method's directory does not exist, or its required files are
missing/misshapen, this script prints a clear warning and SKIPS that
method -- it never fails silently and never aborts the whole run because
one method is unavailable.

Pipeline stages (mirrors scripts/run_candidate_topology_pipeline.sh)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
  0. Input verification: files present, shapes, idx.npy == 0..167, GT
     alignment across methods, finiteness.
  1. VTI generation: writes -speed VTI files under
     ttk_runs_fixed/superlevel_topology/<method>/vti/. Runs inside the same
     phire-ttk:latest Docker image as every other VTI-writing stage in this
     repo, via a hidden --_vti-worker sub-invocation of THIS script (see
     "Do not change existing scripts" below for why this lives here rather
     than in convert_phire_to_vti.py).
  2. TTK PD/MT extraction: ttkPersistenceDiagramCmd / ttkMergeTreeCmd with
     -a wind_speed, --threads 1, resumable (skips already-completed
     fields), one field's Docker failure does not abort the run. Hard gate:
     a method is marked INCOMPLETE (and excluded from distance computation
     and the final report/CSVs) if its VTI/PD/MT counts are not exactly
     336 each (2 * 168 samples).
  3. Distance computation: reuses scripts/compute_composite_tree_distance.py
     unmodified (native python3 + vtk + topologytoolkit), producing
     phase_c_results.csv under
     ttk_runs_fixed/superlevel_topology/<method>/topology/phase_c_final/.
  4. Combined summary: writes the three requested CSVs and the markdown
     report, with a side-by-side comparison against the known completed
     sublevel (default) PD/MT means for the same methods, and a final
     PASS/FAIL discrepancy checklist.

Do not change existing scripts
--------------------------------
convert_phire_to_vti.py has no negation option and is intentionally left
unmodified (it is reused, unmodified, by every existing sublevel pipeline).
Rather than adding a --negate flag to a shared script, the small amount of
VTI-writing code needed here (a near-duplicate of
convert_phire_to_vti.py's make_vti_from_scalar, computing -sqrt(u^2+v^2)
instead of sqrt(u^2+v^2)) lives entirely inside this new script.

Usage (from repo root, on Spark)
-----------------------------------
  Dry run (input verification + planning only; no Docker, no TTK, no
  writes under ttk_runs_fixed/ or docs/):
    python3 scripts/run_superlevel_topology_robustness.py --dry-run

  Full run (writes VTI, runs TTK, computes distances, writes CSVs/report):
    python3 scripts/run_superlevel_topology_robustness.py --run

  Subset of methods:
    python3 scripts/run_superlevel_topology_robustness.py --run \\
      --methods cnn,gan,candidateUV_plus_E2_tf_lowlambda_expanded2688
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import csv
import datetime
import io
import math
import statistics
import subprocess
import sys
from pathlib import Path
from typing import Dict, List, Optional, Tuple

import numpy as np

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repository root
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCRIPT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
REPO_ROOT  = SCRIPT_DIR.parent

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Constants (mirrors scripts/run_candidate_topology_pipeline.sh defaults)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
N_EVAL          = 168
PATCH           = 160
X0              = 0
Y0              = 0
THREADS_DEFAULT = 1
DOCKER_IMAGE    = "phire-ttk:latest"
SCALAR_TOKEN    = "speed"          # filename token only; stored value is -speed
ARRAY_NAME      = "wind_speed"     # VTK array name; TTK is always invoked with -a wind_speed

EXPECTED_SHAPES: Dict[str, Tuple[int, ...]] = {
    "idx.npy":    (N_EVAL,),
    "dataIN.npy": (N_EVAL, 100, 100, 2),
    "dataGT.npy": (N_EVAL, 500, 500, 2),
    "dataSR.npy": (N_EVAL, 500, 500, 2),
}
REQUIRED_FILES = tuple(EXPECTED_SHAPES.keys())

DEFAULT_METHODS: Dict[str, str] = {
    "cnn":                                          "data_out_fixed/wind_mrhr_cnn",
    "gan":                                           "data_out_fixed/wind_mrhr_gan",
    "candidateC_expanded2688":                       "data_out/wind_finetune_candidateC_expanded2688",
    "candidateB_plus_E2_tf_lowlambda_expanded2688":  "data_out/wind_finetune_candidateB_plus_E2_tf_lowlambda_expanded2688",
    "candidateE2_tf_lowlambda_expanded2688":         "data_out/wind_finetune_candidateE2_tf_lowlambda_expanded2688",
    "candidateUV_plus_E2_tf_lowlambda_expanded2688": "data_out/wind_finetune_candidateUV_plus_E2_tf_lowlambda_expanded2688",
    "candidateUV_plus_crit_expanded2688":            "data_out/wind_finetune_candidateUV_plus_crit_expanded2688",
}

# Reference (baseline) method for GT-alignment checks and the winner tables.
REFERENCE_METHOD = "cnn"

# Known completed SUBLEVEL (default) PD/MT means for the same methods, for
# the side-by-side comparison requested in the report. None means "not
# available / not yet run at this scale" -- the report prints "N/A" rather
# than guessing. These are read-only reference numbers; this script never
# touches the sublevel output directories that produced them.
KNOWN_SUBLEVEL: Dict[str, Optional[Dict[str, float]]] = {
    "cnn":                                          {"pd_mean": 27.4063, "mt_mean": 5.8678},
    "gan":                                           {"pd_mean": 20.8641, "mt_mean": 8.3481},
    "candidateC_expanded2688":                       {"pd_mean": 22.4944, "mt_mean": 6.0803},
    "candidateB_plus_E2_tf_lowlambda_expanded2688":  {"pd_mean": 23.9876, "mt_mean": 5.6774},
    "candidateE2_tf_lowlambda_expanded2688":         {"pd_mean": 24.2686, "mt_mean": 5.6628},
    "candidateUV_plus_E2_tf_lowlambda_expanded2688": {"pd_mean": 25.0721, "mt_mean": 5.5940},
    "candidateUV_plus_crit_expanded2688":            {"pd_mean": 29.1143, "mt_mean": 5.6899},
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Output locations
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
OUT_ROOT        = REPO_ROOT / "ttk_runs_fixed" / "superlevel_topology"
REPORT_PATH     = REPO_ROOT / "docs" / "superlevel_topology_robustness_eval.md"
CSV_PER_SAMPLE  = OUT_ROOT / "superlevel_pd_mt_per_sample.csv"
CSV_SUMMARY     = OUT_ROOT / "superlevel_summary_by_method.csv"
CSV_WINNER      = OUT_ROOT / "superlevel_winner_comparison.csv"

# Existing default (sublevel) TTK output roots -- must never be written to.
_PROTECTED_SUBLEVEL_DIRS = [
    REPO_ROOT / "ttk_runs_fixed" / "topology_finetuning",
    REPO_ROOT / "ttk_runs_fixed" / "cnn",
    REPO_ROOT / "ttk_runs_fixed" / "gan",
    REPO_ROOT / "ttk_runs_fixed" / "combined",
]
# Existing candidate/model outputs -- this script only ever reads these.
_PROTECTED_READ_ONLY_DIRS = [
    REPO_ROOT / "data_out_fixed",
    REPO_ROOT / "data_out",
    REPO_ROOT / "models_fixed",
    REPO_ROOT / "models",
]


def _resolve(p: Path) -> Path:
    return p.resolve()


def _is_inside(child: Path, parent: Path) -> bool:
    child = _resolve(child)
    parent = _resolve(parent)
    return child == parent or str(child).startswith(str(parent) + "/")


def _docker_path(p: Path) -> str:
    """Return a path usable inside the Docker container mounted at /work."""
    p = Path(p)
    try:
        return str(p.resolve().relative_to(REPO_ROOT.resolve()))
    except ValueError:
        return str(p)


def method_vti_dir(name: str) -> Path:
    return OUT_ROOT / name / "vti"


def method_topology_dir(name: str) -> Path:
    return OUT_ROOT / name / "topology"


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stage 0: input verification
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

class MethodInputs:
    """Holds the verification outcome and (if ok) the loaded arrays for one
    method."""

    def __init__(self, name: str, data_dir: Path):
        self.name = name
        self.data_dir = data_dir
        self.ok = False
        self.skip_reason: Optional[str] = None
        self.warnings: List[str] = []
        self.idx: Optional[np.ndarray] = None
        self.pos_by_sample: Optional[Dict[int, int]] = None
        # Large arrays are memory-mapped; callers should slice, not load
        # wholesale, except where finiteness/alignment checks require it.
        self.data_gt: Optional[np.ndarray] = None
        self.data_sr: Optional[np.ndarray] = None


def verify_method_inputs(name: str, data_dir: Path) -> MethodInputs:
    m = MethodInputs(name, data_dir)

    if not data_dir.exists():
        m.skip_reason = f"directory not found: {data_dir}"
        print(f"[warn] {name}: {m.skip_reason} -- skipping.")
        return m

    missing = [f for f in REQUIRED_FILES if not (data_dir / f).exists()]
    if missing:
        m.skip_reason = f"missing required file(s): {missing}"
        print(f"[warn] {name}: {m.skip_reason} -- skipping.")
        return m

    shape_errors: List[str] = []
    for fname, expected in EXPECTED_SHAPES.items():
        arr = np.load(data_dir / fname, mmap_mode="r")
        if tuple(arr.shape) != expected:
            shape_errors.append(f"{fname}: got {arr.shape}, expected {expected}")
    if shape_errors:
        m.skip_reason = "shape mismatch: " + "; ".join(shape_errors)
        print(f"[warn] {name}: {m.skip_reason} -- skipping.")
        return m

    idx = np.load(data_dir / "idx.npy").astype(np.int64).ravel()
    if not np.array_equal(np.sort(idx), np.arange(N_EVAL)):
        m.skip_reason = (
            f"idx.npy is not exactly 0..{N_EVAL - 1} "
            f"(range [{int(idx.min())}, {int(idx.max())}], {len(idx)} entries)"
        )
        print(f"[warn] {name}: {m.skip_reason} -- skipping.")
        return m

    data_gt = np.load(data_dir / "dataGT.npy", mmap_mode="r")
    data_sr = np.load(data_dir / "dataSR.npy", mmap_mode="r")

    for label, arr in (("dataGT.npy", data_gt), ("dataSR.npy", data_sr)):
        if not np.isfinite(np.asarray(arr)).all():
            m.skip_reason = f"{label} contains NaN/inf values"
            print(f"[warn] {name}: {m.skip_reason} -- skipping.")
            return m

    m.idx = idx
    m.pos_by_sample = {int(v): i for i, v in enumerate(idx)}
    m.data_gt = data_gt
    m.data_sr = data_sr
    m.ok = True
    print(f"[ok]   {name}: files present, shapes OK, idx == 0..{N_EVAL - 1}, arrays finite.")
    return m


def check_gt_alignment(methods: Dict[str, MethodInputs], reference: str) -> List[str]:
    """Compare every ok method's dataGT (in sample-idx order) against the
    reference method's dataGT. Returns a list of warning strings; does not
    raise. If the reference method itself is unavailable, the first
    available ok method is used instead."""
    warnings: List[str] = []
    ok_methods = {n: m for n, m in methods.items() if m.ok}
    if not ok_methods:
        return ["no methods available -- GT alignment check skipped"]

    ref_name = reference if reference in ok_methods else next(iter(ok_methods))
    if ref_name != reference:
        warnings.append(
            f"reference method {reference!r} unavailable; using {ref_name!r} "
            "as the GT-alignment reference instead"
        )
    ref = ok_methods[ref_name]
    ref_order = np.array([ref.pos_by_sample[s] for s in range(N_EVAL)])
    ref_gt = np.asarray(ref.data_gt)[ref_order].astype(np.float64)

    for name, m in ok_methods.items():
        if name == ref_name:
            continue
        order = np.array([m.pos_by_sample[s] for s in range(N_EVAL)])
        gt = np.asarray(m.data_gt)[order].astype(np.float64)
        max_diff = float(np.abs(gt - ref_gt).max())
        if max_diff > 1e-3:
            warnings.append(
                f"{name}: dataGT differs from {ref_name} by up to {max_diff:.4e} "
                "(possible misalignment or different normalization)"
            )
        else:
            print(f"[ok]   {name}: dataGT aligned with {ref_name} (max_abs_diff={max_diff:.2e}).")
    return warnings


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VTI writer (worker mode; runs natively OR inside Docker via --_vti-worker)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def _make_vti_from_scalar(scalar_2d: np.ndarray, array_name: str, out_vti: Path) -> None:
    """Write a 2D scalar field as ASCII VTK ImageData (.vti).

    Identical convention to scripts/convert_phire_to_vti.py's
    make_vti_from_scalar(): scalar_2d[y, x] -> VTK point (x, y), C-order
    ravel so flat[ix + iy*W] == scalar_2d[iy, ix].
    """
    import vtk  # local import: not needed for --dry-run / orchestration
    from vtk.util.numpy_support import numpy_to_vtk

    scalar_2d = np.asarray(scalar_2d, dtype=np.float32)
    if scalar_2d.ndim != 2:
        raise ValueError(f"Expected 2D scalar, got shape {scalar_2d.shape}")
    H, W = scalar_2d.shape

    img = vtk.vtkImageData()
    img.SetDimensions(W, H, 1)
    img.SetExtent(0, W - 1, 0, H - 1, 0, 0)
    img.SetSpacing(1.0, 1.0, 1.0)
    img.SetOrigin(0.0, 0.0, 0.0)

    flat = np.ascontiguousarray(scalar_2d).ravel(order="C")
    vtk_arr = numpy_to_vtk(flat, deep=True, array_type=vtk.VTK_FLOAT)
    vtk_arr.SetName(array_name)

    pd = img.GetPointData()
    pd.AddArray(vtk_arr)
    pd.SetActiveScalars(array_name)
    pd.SetScalars(vtk_arr)

    w = vtk.vtkXMLImageDataWriter()
    w.SetFileName(str(out_vti))
    w.SetInputData(img)
    w.SetDataModeToAscii()

    ok = w.Write()
    if not ok:
        raise RuntimeError(f"VTK failed to write {out_vti}")


def _crop(field: np.ndarray, patch: int, x0: int, y0: int) -> np.ndarray:
    if not patch:
        return field
    H, W = field.shape
    x1 = min(x0 + patch, W)
    y1 = min(y0 + patch, H)
    return field[y0:y1, x0:x1]


def _negated_speed(sample_hw2: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
    """sample_hw2: (H, W, 2) array of [u, v]. Returns -sqrt(u^2 + v^2)."""
    u = sample_hw2[..., 0].astype(np.float32)
    v = sample_hw2[..., 1].astype(np.float32)
    return -np.sqrt(u * u + v * v)


def vti_worker_main(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:
    """Entry point when invoked as --_vti-worker (typically inside Docker).
    Writes one VTI per requested sample index from a single .npy file."""
    in_path = Path(args.input)
    outdir = Path(args.outdir)
    outdir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    label = args.label

    arr = np.load(in_path, mmap_mode="r")
    if arr.ndim != 4 or arr.shape[-1] < 2:
        print(f"[error] --_vti-worker: unexpected array shape {arr.shape} in {in_path}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1

    patch_tag = f"p{PATCH}_x{X0}_y{Y0}" if PATCH else "full"
    n_written = 0
    for sidx in args.samples:
        sample = np.asarray(arr[sidx])  # (H, W, 2)
        u = _crop(sample[..., 0], PATCH, X0, Y0)
        v = _crop(sample[..., 1], PATCH, X0, Y0)
        neg_speed = -np.sqrt(u.astype(np.float32) ** 2 + v.astype(np.float32) ** 2)
        out_vti = outdir / f"{label}_s{sidx}_{SCALAR_TOKEN}_{patch_tag}.vti"
        _make_vti_from_scalar(neg_speed, ARRAY_NAME, out_vti)
        n_written += 1
    print(f"[_vti-worker] wrote {n_written} VTI file(s) to {outdir} (label={label})")
    return 0


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stage 1: VTI generation (host-side orchestration; delegates to Docker)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def _docker_run(cmd_inner: str, extra_env: Optional[Dict[str, str]] = None) -> int:
    docker_cmd = ["docker", "run", "--rm", "-v", f"{REPO_ROOT}:/work", "-w", "/work"]
    for k, v in (extra_env or {}).items():
        docker_cmd += ["-e", f"{k}={v}"]
    docker_cmd += [DOCKER_IMAGE, "bash", "-lc", cmd_inner]
    print(f"  $ {' '.join(docker_cmd)}")
    proc = subprocess.run(docker_cmd, cwd=REPO_ROOT)
    return proc.returncode


def generate_vti_for_method(name: str, m: MethodInputs, dry_run: bool) -> bool:
    """Generate negated-speed VTI files natively on the host.

    Earlier versions delegated this stage to Docker. That made the VTI stage
    sensitive to host-vs-container path conventions and to the Python packages
    installed inside phire-ttk:latest. Since the host Python environment has
    vtk/numpy available, VTI writing is safer natively. TTK extraction still
    runs through Docker below.
    """
    vti_dir = method_vti_dir(name)
    sample_args = [str(i) for i in range(N_EVAL)]
    ok = True

    for which, npy_file in (("GT", "dataGT.npy"), ("SR", "dataSR.npy")):
        label = f"{name}_{which}"
        existing = list(vti_dir.glob(f"{label}_s*_{SCALAR_TOKEN}_*.vti")) if vti_dir.exists() else []
        if len(existing) == N_EVAL:
            print(f"  [skip] {label}: {len(existing)}/{N_EVAL} VTI files already present.")
            continue

        cmd = [
            "python3",
            "scripts/run_superlevel_topology_robustness.py",
            "--_vti-worker",
            "--input", str(m.data_dir / npy_file),
            "--outdir", str(vti_dir),
            "--label", label,
            "--samples",
            *sample_args,
        ]

        if dry_run:
            print(f"  [dry-run] would generate {N_EVAL} VTI files for {label} natively:")
            print("    " + " ".join(cmd))
            continue

        vti_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        print(f"  === VTI generation: {label} ===")
        print("  $ " + " ".join(cmd))
        proc = subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=REPO_ROOT)
        if proc.returncode != 0:
            print(f"  [warn] VTI generation failed for {label} (exit code {proc.returncode}).")
            ok = False

    return ok



# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stage 2: TTK PD/MT extraction (mirrors run_candidate_topology_pipeline.sh)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def _pd_output_exists(pd_dir: Path, base: str) -> bool:
    for loc in (pd_dir, pd_dir / "GT", pd_dir / "SR"):
        if (loc / f"{base}_pd_port_0.vtu").exists():
            return True
    return False


def _mt_output_exists(mt_dir: Path, base: str) -> bool:
    for loc in (mt_dir, mt_dir / "GT", mt_dir / "SR"):
        if (
            (loc / f"{base}_mt_port_0.vtu").exists()
            and (loc / f"{base}_mt_port_1.vtu").exists()
            and (loc / f"{base}_mt_port_2.vti").exists()
        ):
            return True
    return False


def run_ttk_extraction(name: str, threads: int, dry_run: bool) -> Tuple[bool, Dict[str, int]]:
    vti_dir = method_vti_dir(name)
    topo_dir = method_topology_dir(name)
    pd_dir = topo_dir / "pd"
    mt_dir = topo_dir / "mt"

    vti_files = sorted(vti_dir.glob(f"{name}_*.vti")) if vti_dir.exists() else []
    counts = {"vti": len(vti_files), "pd": 0, "mt_port0": 0, "mt_port1": 0, "mt_port2": 0}

    if not vti_files:
        print(f"  [error] {name}: no VTI files found in {vti_dir} matching {name}_*.vti")
        return False, counts

    if dry_run:
        print(f"  [dry-run] would run TTK PD+MT extraction on {len(vti_files)} VTI files "
              f"(threads={threads}), writing under {topo_dir}")
        return True, counts

    for d in (pd_dir, pd_dir / "GT", pd_dir / "SR", mt_dir, mt_dir / "GT", mt_dir / "SR"):
        d.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)

    env = {"OMP_NUM_THREADS": str(threads), "TTK_NUM_THREADS": str(threads)}

    for f in vti_files:
        base = f.stem
        if not _pd_output_exists(pd_dir, base):
            print(f"  === PD: {base} ===")
            rc = _docker_run(
                f"ttkPersistenceDiagramCmd -t {threads} -i {_docker_path(f)} -a {ARRAY_NAME} -o {_docker_path(pd_dir / (base + '_pd'))}",
                extra_env=env,
            )
            if rc != 0:
                print(f"  [warn] PD failed for {base} (docker exit code {rc}). Will retry on next run.")
        else:
            print(f"  [skip] PD {base}")

        if not _mt_output_exists(mt_dir, base):
            print(f"  === MT: {base} ===")
            rc = _docker_run(
                f"ttkMergeTreeCmd -t {threads} -i {_docker_path(f)} -a {ARRAY_NAME} -o {_docker_path(mt_dir / (base + '_mt'))}",
                extra_env=env,
            )
            if rc != 0:
                print(f"  [warn] MT failed for {base} (docker exit code {rc}). Will retry on next run.")
        else:
            print(f"  [skip] MT {base}")

    # Organise top-level GT/SR-labelled outputs into GT/ and SR/ subdirs.
    for src_dir, dst_root in ((pd_dir, pd_dir), (mt_dir, mt_dir)):
        for which in ("GT", "SR"):
            for p in list(src_dir.glob(f"{name}_{which}_*")):
                if p.is_file():
                    p.rename(dst_root / which / p.name)

    counts["pd"] = len(list(pd_dir.rglob("*_pd_port_0.vtu")))
    counts["mt_port0"] = len(list(mt_dir.rglob("*_mt_port_0.vtu")))
    counts["mt_port1"] = len(list(mt_dir.rglob("*_mt_port_1.vtu")))
    counts["mt_port2"] = len(list(mt_dir.rglob("*_mt_port_2.vti")))

    expected = 2 * N_EVAL
    complete = (
        counts["pd"] == expected
        and counts["mt_port0"] == expected
        and counts["mt_port1"] == expected
        and counts["mt_port2"] == expected
    )
    if not complete:
        print(f"  [error] {name}: TTK extraction incomplete: "
              f"PD={counts['pd']}/{expected}  "
              f"MT p0={counts['mt_port0']}/{expected}  "
              f"p1={counts['mt_port1']}/{expected}  "
              f"p2={counts['mt_port2']}/{expected}. "
              f"Hard-failing this method (no distance computation); re-run to retry only "
              f"missing/failed fields (already-completed fields are skipped, not recomputed).")
    return complete, counts


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stage 3: distance computation (reuses compute_composite_tree_distance.py)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def run_distance_computation(name: str, dry_run: bool) -> Optional[Path]:
    topo_dir = method_topology_dir(name)
    pd_dir = topo_dir / "pd"
    mt_dir = topo_dir / "mt"
    final_dir = topo_dir / "phase_c_final"
    results_csv = final_dir / "phase_c_results.csv"

    if dry_run:
        print(f"  [dry-run] would compute PD/MT distances for {name} -> {results_csv}")
        return None

    if results_csv.exists():
        print(f"  [skip] {name}: {results_csv} already exists.")
        return results_csv

    cmd = [
        "python3", "-X", "faulthandler", "scripts/compute_composite_tree_distance.py",
        "--pd-dir", str(pd_dir), "--mt-dir", str(mt_dir), "--outdir", str(final_dir),
        "--isolate-mt",
    ]
    print(f"  $ {' '.join(cmd)}")
    proc = subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=REPO_ROOT)
    if proc.returncode != 0:
        print(f"  [error] distance computation failed for {name} (exit code {proc.returncode}).")
        return None
    if not results_csv.exists():
        print(f"  [error] {results_csv} not written despite exit code 0.")
        return None
    return results_csv


_KEY_POS_RE = None  # set lazily to avoid importing re at module scope twice


def _parse_pos_idx(key: str) -> Optional[int]:
    import re
    global _KEY_POS_RE
    if _KEY_POS_RE is None:
        _KEY_POS_RE = re.compile(r"_s(\d+)_")
    m = _KEY_POS_RE.search(key)
    return int(m.group(1)) if m else None


def load_phase_c_results(csv_path: Path, method_filter: str) -> Dict[int, Tuple[float, float]]:
    """Return {pos_idx: (pd_distance, mt_distance)} for rows whose `method`
    column matches method_filter exactly (case-sensitive) -- this is the
    'confirm no report accidentally references the wrong method name'
    safety check applied at parse time: rows for any other method in the
    same CSV are ignored rather than merged in."""
    out: Dict[int, Tuple[float, float]] = {}
    with csv_path.open() as fh:
        for row in csv.DictReader(fh):
            method = (row.get("method") or "").strip()
            if method != method_filter:
                continue
            pos = _parse_pos_idx((row.get("key") or "").strip())
            if pos is None:
                continue
            try:
                pd_v = float(row.get("pd_distance") or "nan")
            except ValueError:
                pd_v = float("nan")
            try:
                mt_v = float(row.get("mt_distance") or "nan")
            except ValueError:
                mt_v = float("nan")
            out[pos] = (pd_v, mt_v)
    return out


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stage 4: combined CSVs + report
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def _mean(vals: List[float]) -> float:
    v = [x for x in vals if not math.isnan(x)]
    return sum(v) / len(v) if v else float("nan")


def _std(vals: List[float]) -> float:
    v = [x for x in vals if not math.isnan(x)]
    return statistics.pstdev(v) if len(v) > 1 else float("nan")


def _fmt(v: Optional[float], d: int = 4) -> str:
    if v is None or (isinstance(v, float) and math.isnan(v)):
        return "N/A"
    return f"{v:.{d}f}"


def build_outputs(
    method_results: Dict[str, Dict[int, Tuple[float, float]]],
    methods_run: List[str],
) -> Tuple[bool, List[str]]:
    """Build the three CSVs and the markdown report from completed
    per-method phase_c_results.csv data. Returns (all_ok, checklist_lines)."""
    checklist: List[str] = []
    all_ok = True

    def _check(label: str, ok: bool) -> None:
        nonlocal all_ok
        checklist.append(f"[{'PASS' if ok else 'FAIL'}] {label}")
        if not ok:
            all_ok = False

    completed = [m for m in methods_run if m in method_results and method_results[m]]
    _check("At least one method has completed distance results", len(completed) > 0)
    if not completed:
        return all_ok, checklist

    # --- per-sample CSV (long format: one row per method per sample) ------
    per_sample_rows: List[Dict[str, object]] = []
    for name in completed:
        dists = method_results[name]
        n_rows_this_method = 0
        for pos in sorted(dists):
            pd_v, mt_v = dists[pos]
            per_sample_rows.append({
                "method": name,
                "pos_idx": pos,
                "sample_idx": pos,  # idx.npy == 0..167 in identity order for all verified methods
                "pd_distance_superlevel": pd_v,
                "mt_distance_superlevel": mt_v,
            })
            n_rows_this_method += 1
        _check(f"{name}: per-sample CSV row count == {N_EVAL}", n_rows_this_method == N_EVAL)

    OUT_ROOT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    with CSV_PER_SAMPLE.open("w", newline="") as fh:
        w = csv.DictWriter(fh, fieldnames=["method", "pos_idx", "sample_idx",
                                            "pd_distance_superlevel", "mt_distance_superlevel"])
        w.writeheader()
        w.writerows(per_sample_rows)
    print(f"Written: {CSV_PER_SAMPLE}")

    # --- per-method summary stats -------------------------------------------
    pd_by_method: Dict[str, List[float]] = {}
    mt_by_method: Dict[str, List[float]] = {}
    for name in completed:
        dists = method_results[name]
        pd_by_method[name] = [dists[p][0] for p in sorted(dists)]
        mt_by_method[name] = [dists[p][1] for p in sorted(dists)]

    cnn_pd = pd_by_method.get(REFERENCE_METHOD)
    cnn_mt = mt_by_method.get(REFERENCE_METHOD)
    gan_pd = pd_by_method.get("gan")
    gan_mt = mt_by_method.get("gan")

    def _lt_count(cand: Optional[List[float]], base: Optional[List[float]]) -> Optional[int]:
        if cand is None or base is None or len(cand) != len(base):
            return None
        return sum(1 for c, b in zip(cand, base) if not (math.isnan(c) or math.isnan(b)) and c < b)

    # Freshly-computed superlevel MT-GAN win set (samples where GAN's
    # superlevel MT distance beats CNN's superlevel MT distance), analogous
    # to the hardcoded 20-sample set used throughout the sublevel reports
    # but recomputed here from this run's own cnn/gan data.
    mt_gan_wins: set = set()
    if REFERENCE_METHOD in method_results and "gan" in method_results:
        cnn_d = method_results[REFERENCE_METHOD]
        gan_d = method_results["gan"]
        for pos in cnn_d:
            if pos in gan_d:
                c_mt = cnn_d[pos][1]
                g_mt = gan_d[pos][1]
                if not (math.isnan(c_mt) or math.isnan(g_mt)) and g_mt < c_mt:
                    mt_gan_wins.add(pos)

    summary_rows: List[Dict[str, object]] = []
    mt_gan_recovery: Dict[str, Dict[str, int]] = {}
    for name in completed:
        pd_vals = pd_by_method[name]
        mt_vals = mt_by_method[name]
        pd_mean_v = _mean(pd_vals)
        mt_mean_v = _mean(mt_vals)
        pd_lt_cnn = _lt_count(pd_vals, cnn_pd) if name != REFERENCE_METHOD else None
        mt_lt_cnn = _lt_count(mt_vals, cnn_mt) if name != REFERENCE_METHOD else None
        pd_beats_gan = _lt_count(pd_vals, gan_pd) if name not in (REFERENCE_METHOD, "gan") else None
        mt_beats_gan = _lt_count(mt_vals, gan_mt) if name not in (REFERENCE_METHOD, "gan") else None

        recovered = still_gan = now_cnn = 0
        if name not in (REFERENCE_METHOD, "gan") and mt_gan_wins:
            dists = method_results[name]
            cnn_d = method_results.get(REFERENCE_METHOD, {})
            gan_d = method_results.get("gan", {})
            for pos in mt_gan_wins:
                if pos not in dists or pos not in cnn_d or pos not in gan_d:
                    continue
                vals = {REFERENCE_METHOD: cnn_d[pos][1], "gan": gan_d[pos][1], name: dists[pos][1]}
                valid = {k: v for k, v in vals.items() if not math.isnan(v)}
                if not valid:
                    continue
                winner = min(valid, key=valid.get)
                if winner == name:
                    recovered += 1
                elif winner == "gan":
                    still_gan += 1
                elif winner == REFERENCE_METHOD:
                    now_cnn += 1
            mt_gan_recovery[name] = {"recovered": recovered, "still_gan": still_gan, "now_cnn": now_cnn}

        known = KNOWN_SUBLEVEL.get(name)
        summary_rows.append({
            "method": name,
            "n_samples": len(pd_vals),
            "pd_mean_superlevel": pd_mean_v,
            "pd_std_superlevel": _std(pd_vals),
            "mt_mean_superlevel": mt_mean_v,
            "mt_std_superlevel": _std(mt_vals),
            "pd_lt_cnn": pd_lt_cnn if pd_lt_cnn is not None else "",
            "mt_lt_cnn": mt_lt_cnn if mt_lt_cnn is not None else "",
            "pd_beats_gan": pd_beats_gan if pd_beats_gan is not None else "",
            "mt_beats_gan": mt_beats_gan if mt_beats_gan is not None else "",
            "mt_gan_recovered": mt_gan_recovery.get(name, {}).get("recovered", ""),
            "mt_gan_total": len(mt_gan_wins) if mt_gan_wins else "",
            "pd_mean_sublevel_known": known["pd_mean"] if known else "",
            "mt_mean_sublevel_known": known["mt_mean"] if known else "",
        })

    with CSV_SUMMARY.open("w", newline="") as fh:
        w = csv.DictWriter(fh, fieldnames=list(summary_rows[0].keys()))
        w.writeheader()
        w.writerows(summary_rows)
    print(f"Written: {CSV_SUMMARY}")

    # --- per-sample winner CSV ----------------------------------------------
    winner_rows: List[Dict[str, object]] = []
    for pos in range(N_EVAL):
        pd_candidates = {n: method_results[n][pos][0] for n in completed
                          if pos in method_results[n] and not math.isnan(method_results[n][pos][0])}
        mt_candidates = {n: method_results[n][pos][1] for n in completed
                          if pos in method_results[n] and not math.isnan(method_results[n][pos][1])}
        pd_winner = min(pd_candidates, key=pd_candidates.get) if pd_candidates else "N/A"
        mt_winner = min(mt_candidates, key=mt_candidates.get) if mt_candidates else "N/A"
        winner_rows.append({
            "sample_idx": pos,
            "pos_idx": pos,
            "pd_winner_superlevel": pd_winner,
            "mt_winner_superlevel": mt_winner,
            "was_mt_gan_win_superlevel_baseline": int(pos in mt_gan_wins),
        })
    _check(f"Winner CSV row count == {N_EVAL}", len(winner_rows) == N_EVAL)

    with CSV_WINNER.open("w", newline="") as fh:
        w = csv.DictWriter(fh, fieldnames=list(winner_rows[0].keys()))
        w.writeheader()
        w.writerows(winner_rows)
    print(f"Written: {CSV_WINNER}")

    # --- markdown report ------------------------------------------------------
    md = io.StringIO()
    md.write("# Superlevel topology robustness evaluation\n\n")
    md.write(f"**Generated:** {datetime.date.today().isoformat()}\n\n")
    md.write(
        "**Method:** superlevel topology of speed `s` is computed as sublevel "
        "topology of `-s`, using the unmodified TTK `ttkPersistenceDiagramCmd`/"
        "`ttkMergeTreeCmd` commands on VTI files whose `wind_speed` array stores "
        "`-sqrt(u^2+v^2)` (negated speed), not speed. No existing sublevel/default "
        "topology output was read, modified, or overwritten, and no model was "
        "retrained. All outputs live under `ttk_runs_fixed/superlevel_topology/`.\n\n"
    )
    md.write("**Note: lower PD/MT distance is better for both metrics, in both the "
              "superlevel and sublevel evaluations.**\n\n")
    md.write(f"**Samples evaluated per method:** {N_EVAL}\n\n")
    md.write(f"**Methods completed:** {', '.join(completed)}\n\n")
    skipped = [m for m in methods_run if m not in completed]
    if skipped:
        md.write(f"**Methods skipped/incomplete:** {', '.join(skipped)} "
                 "(see console log / PASS-FAIL checklist for reasons)\n\n")
    if mt_gan_wins:
        md.write(f"**Superlevel MT-GAN baseline wins (GAN beats CNN on superlevel MT):** "
                  f"{len(mt_gan_wins)} samples — {sorted(mt_gan_wins)}\n\n")

    md.write("## Mean PD / MT by method (superlevel)\n\n")
    md.write("| Method | PD mean (superlevel) | MT mean (superlevel) | PD mean (sublevel, known) | "
              "MT mean (sublevel, known) |\n")
    md.write("|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n")
    for r in summary_rows:
        md.write(f"| {r['method']} | {_fmt(r['pd_mean_superlevel'])} | {_fmt(r['mt_mean_superlevel'])} "
                  f"| {_fmt(r['pd_mean_sublevel_known'] if r['pd_mean_sublevel_known'] != '' else None)} "
                  f"| {_fmt(r['mt_mean_sublevel_known'] if r['mt_mean_sublevel_known'] != '' else None)} |\n")
    md.write("\n")

    md.write("## PD / MT wins vs CNN, beats-GAN counts (superlevel)\n\n")
    md.write(f"| Method | PD < CNN | MT < CNN | PD beats GAN | MT beats GAN | "
              f"MT-GAN recovered (/{len(mt_gan_wins)}) |\n")
    md.write("|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n")
    for r in summary_rows:
        md.write(f"| {r['method']} "
                  f"| {r['pd_lt_cnn'] if r['pd_lt_cnn'] != '' else '--'}/{N_EVAL} "
                  f"| {r['mt_lt_cnn'] if r['mt_lt_cnn'] != '' else '--'}/{N_EVAL} "
                  f"| {r['pd_beats_gan'] if r['pd_beats_gan'] != '' else '--'}/{N_EVAL} "
                  f"| {r['mt_beats_gan'] if r['mt_beats_gan'] != '' else '--'}/{N_EVAL} "
                  f"| {r['mt_gan_recovered'] if r['mt_gan_recovered'] != '' else '--'} |\n")
    md.write("\n")

    md.write("## Winner distribution (superlevel)\n\n")
    for label, col in (("PD", "pd_winner_superlevel"), ("MT", "mt_winner_superlevel")):
        counts: Dict[str, int] = {}
        for r in winner_rows:
            counts[r[col]] = counts.get(r[col], 0) + 1
        md.write(f"### {label} distance winners\n\n")
        md.write("| Method | Wins |\n|---|---:|\n")
        for name, c in sorted(counts.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1]):
            md.write(f"| {name} | {c} |\n")
        md.write("\n")

    if mt_gan_wins:
        md.write("## MT-GAN recovery detail (superlevel)\n\n")
        md.write(f"Samples where GAN's superlevel MT distance beat CNN's superlevel MT "
                  f"distance: {sorted(mt_gan_wins)}\n\n")
        md.write("| Method | Recovered (winner becomes method) | Still GAN | Now CNN |\n")
        md.write("|---|---:|---:|---:|\n")
        for name, d in mt_gan_recovery.items():
            md.write(f"| {name} | {d['recovered']} | {d['still_gan']} | {d['now_cnn']} |\n")
        md.write("\n")

    md.write("## Superlevel vs sublevel side-by-side (known values)\n\n")
    md.write("| Method | PD superlevel | PD sublevel (known) | MT superlevel | MT sublevel (known) |\n")
    md.write("|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n")
    for r in summary_rows:
        md.write(f"| {r['method']} | {_fmt(r['pd_mean_superlevel'])} "
                  f"| {_fmt(r['pd_mean_sublevel_known'] if r['pd_mean_sublevel_known'] != '' else None)} "
                  f"| {_fmt(r['mt_mean_superlevel'])} "
                  f"| {_fmt(r['mt_mean_sublevel_known'] if r['mt_mean_sublevel_known'] != '' else None)} |\n")
    md.write("\n")

    md.write("## Output files\n\n")
    md.write(f"- `{CSV_PER_SAMPLE.relative_to(REPO_ROOT)}` — per-sample PD/MT distances, one row per (method, sample)\n")
    md.write(f"- `{CSV_SUMMARY.relative_to(REPO_ROOT)}` — per-method summary statistics\n")
    md.write(f"- `{CSV_WINNER.relative_to(REPO_ROOT)}` — per-sample PD/MT winner across all completed methods\n")
    md.write(f"- `{REPORT_PATH.relative_to(REPO_ROOT)}` — this report\n\n")

    md.write("## Notes\n\n")
    md.write("- PD distance = bottleneck distance between persistence diagrams "
              "(`ttkBottleneckDistance`), computed on the negated (`-speed`) scalar field.\n")
    md.write("- MT distance = Wasserstein-type merge tree distance "
              "(`ttkMergeTreeDistanceMatrix`), computed on the negated (`-speed`) scalar field.\n")
    md.write("- Both use 160x160 speed patches at (x0=0, y0=0), matching the sublevel baseline convention.\n")
    md.write("- **Lower distance is better for both metrics, in both the superlevel and sublevel domains.**\n")
    md.write("- Existing sublevel/default topology outputs and all candidate data_out*/models*/ "
              "outputs were never read for writing, modified, or overwritten by this script.\n")
    md.write("- No model was retrained to produce this evaluation.\n")

    REPORT_PATH.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    REPORT_PATH.write_text(md.getvalue(), encoding="utf-8")
    print(f"Written: {REPORT_PATH}")

    return all_ok, checklist


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Safety / discrepancy checks
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def run_safety_checks() -> List[str]:
    lines: List[str] = []

    def _check(label: str, ok: bool) -> None:
        lines.append(f"[{'PASS' if ok else 'FAIL'}] {label}")

    for d in _PROTECTED_SUBLEVEL_DIRS:
        _check(f"OUT_ROOT does not overlap protected sublevel dir {d.relative_to(REPO_ROOT)}",
               not _is_inside(OUT_ROOT, d) and not _is_inside(d, OUT_ROOT))
    for d in _PROTECTED_READ_ONLY_DIRS:
        _check(f"OUT_ROOT does not overlap read-only data dir {d.relative_to(REPO_ROOT)}",
               not _is_inside(OUT_ROOT, d))
    _check("OUT_ROOT resolves under ttk_runs_fixed/superlevel_topology",
           _is_inside(OUT_ROOT, REPO_ROOT / "ttk_runs_fixed" / "superlevel_topology"))
    _check("REPORT_PATH resolves under docs/", _is_inside(REPORT_PATH, REPO_ROOT / "docs"))
    for csv_path in (CSV_PER_SAMPLE, CSV_SUMMARY, CSV_WINNER):
        _check(f"{csv_path.name} resolves under OUT_ROOT", _is_inside(csv_path, OUT_ROOT))

    return lines


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Orchestration
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def _parse_args() -> argparse.Namespace:
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter
    )
    mode = ap.add_mutually_exclusive_group()
    mode.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true",
                       help="Verify inputs and print the plan; no Docker/TTK calls, no writes.")
    mode.add_argument("--run", action="store_true",
                       help="Execute the full pipeline (VTI + TTK + distances + report).")
    ap.add_argument("--methods", default=None,
                     help="Comma-separated subset of method names to evaluate "
                          "(default: all of DEFAULT_METHODS).")
    ap.add_argument("--threads", type=int, default=THREADS_DEFAULT,
                     help=f"TTK thread count per Docker call (default: {THREADS_DEFAULT}).")

    # Hidden worker mode (invoked recursively, typically inside Docker).
    ap.add_argument("--_vti-worker", action="store_true", help=argparse.SUPPRESS)
    ap.add_argument("--input", default=None, help=argparse.SUPPRESS)
    ap.add_argument("--outdir", default=None, help=argparse.SUPPRESS)
    ap.add_argument("--label", default=None, help=argparse.SUPPRESS)
    ap.add_argument("--samples", type=int, nargs="+", default=None, help=argparse.SUPPRESS)

    return ap.parse_args()


def main() -> int:
    args = _parse_args()

    if getattr(args, "_vti_worker"):
        return vti_worker_main(args)

    if not args.dry_run and not args.run:
        print("[error] exactly one of --dry-run or --run is required.")
        return 2

    dry_run = bool(args.dry_run)

    if args.methods:
        requested = [s.strip() for s in args.methods.split(",") if s.strip()]
        unknown = [r for r in requested if r not in DEFAULT_METHODS]
        if unknown:
            print(f"[error] unknown method name(s) in --methods: {unknown}. "
                  f"Known methods: {sorted(DEFAULT_METHODS)}")
            return 2
        methods = {r: DEFAULT_METHODS[r] for r in requested}
    else:
        methods = dict(DEFAULT_METHODS)

    print("=" * 72)
    print(f"Superlevel topology robustness evaluation ({'DRY RUN' if dry_run else 'RUN'})")
    print("=" * 72)
    print(f"  Methods requested : {list(methods)}")
    print(f"  Output root       : {OUT_ROOT}")
    print(f"  Report path       : {REPORT_PATH}")
    print(f"  Threads           : {args.threads}")
    print("=" * 72)
    print()

    print("--- Safety checks ---")
    safety_lines = run_safety_checks()
    for line in safety_lines:
        print(f"  {line}")
    if any(l.startswith("[FAIL]") for l in safety_lines):
        print("[error] safety checks failed; aborting before touching any output path.")
        return 1
    print()

    print("--- Stage 0: input verification ---")
    verified: Dict[str, MethodInputs] = {}
    for name, rel_dir in methods.items():
        verified[name] = verify_method_inputs(name, REPO_ROOT / rel_dir)
    print()

    print("--- GT alignment across methods ---")
    align_warnings = check_gt_alignment(verified, REFERENCE_METHOD)
    for w in align_warnings:
        print(f"  [warn] {w}")
    print()

    ok_methods = [n for n, m in verified.items() if m.ok]
    if not ok_methods:
        print("[warn] no methods passed input verification -- nothing to evaluate.")
        print()
        checklist = [f"[{'FAIL'}] at least one method available"] + safety_lines
        print("--- Final PASS/FAIL checklist ---")
        for line in checklist:
            print(f"  {line}")
        return 0 if dry_run else 1

    if dry_run:
        print("--- Stage 1-3 plan (dry-run; nothing executed) ---")
        for name in ok_methods:
            vti_dir = method_vti_dir(name)
            topo_dir = method_topology_dir(name)
            print(f"  {name}:")
            print(f"    VTI dir      : {vti_dir}  (would write {2 * N_EVAL} files: "
                  f"{N_EVAL} GT + {N_EVAL} SR, each storing -speed)")
            print(f"    Topology dir : {topo_dir}")
            print(f"    Expect       : VTI={2 * N_EVAL} PD={2 * N_EVAL} "
                  f"MT_port0={2 * N_EVAL} MT_port1={2 * N_EVAL} MT_port2={2 * N_EVAL}")
        print()
        print("--- Final PASS/FAIL checklist (dry-run) ---")
        checklist = safety_lines + [f"[PASS] input verification: {name}" for name in ok_methods]
        checklist += [f"[SKIP-dry-run] {name}: VTI/TTK/distance stages not executed" for name in ok_methods]
        for line in checklist:
            print(f"  {line}")
        print()
        print("Dry run complete. No Docker/TTK calls were made; no files were written "
              "under ttk_runs_fixed/ or docs/.")
        return 0

    # --run mode below this point.
    method_results: Dict[str, Dict[int, Tuple[float, float]]] = {}
    stage_checklist: List[str] = list(safety_lines)

    for name in ok_methods:
        print(f"--- {name}: Stage 1 (VTI generation) ---")
        vti_ok = generate_vti_for_method(name, verified[name], dry_run=False)
        stage_checklist.append(f"[{'PASS' if vti_ok else 'FAIL'}] {name}: VTI generation")

        print(f"--- {name}: Stage 2 (TTK PD/MT extraction) ---")
        extraction_ok, counts = run_ttk_extraction(name, threads=args.threads, dry_run=False)
        stage_checklist.append(
            f"[{'PASS' if extraction_ok else 'FAIL'}] {name}: complete TTK outputs "
            f"(VTI={counts['vti']} PD={counts['pd']} MT_p0={counts['mt_port0']} "
            f"MT_p1={counts['mt_port1']} MT_p2={counts['mt_port2']}, expect {2 * N_EVAL} each)"
        )
        if not (vti_ok and extraction_ok):
            print(f"  [error] {name}: hard-failing (VTI/TTK stage incomplete); "
                  "skipping distance computation for this method.")
            continue

        print(f"--- {name}: Stage 3 (distance computation) ---")
        results_csv = run_distance_computation(name, dry_run=False)
        if results_csv is None:
            stage_checklist.append(f"[FAIL] {name}: distance computation")
            continue
        stage_checklist.append(f"[PASS] {name}: distance computation")

        dists = load_phase_c_results(results_csv, method_filter=name)
        stage_checklist.append(
            f"[{'PASS' if len(dists) == N_EVAL else 'FAIL'}] {name}: "
            f"phase_c_results.csv row count for method={name!r} == {N_EVAL} (got {len(dists)})"
        )
        method_results[name] = dists
        print()

    print("--- Stage 4: combined CSVs + report ---")
    outputs_ok, outputs_checklist = build_outputs(method_results, ok_methods)
    stage_checklist += outputs_checklist
    print()

    print("--- Final PASS/FAIL checklist ---")
    for line in stage_checklist:
        print(f"  {line}")

    overall_ok = all(l.startswith("[PASS]") or l.startswith("[SKIP") for l in stage_checklist)
    print()
    print("Superlevel topology robustness evaluation "
          f"{'COMPLETE (all checks passed)' if overall_ok else 'FINISHED WITH FAILURES'}.")
    return 0 if overall_ok else 1


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
